{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00214",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 4.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Excuse me, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.74,
      "end_seconds": 10.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.29,
      "end_seconds": 17.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Well, I've been having tightness in my chest when I walk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.7,
      "end_seconds": 21.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.19,
      "end_seconds": 25.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I've had it for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.88,
      "end_seconds": 30.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.19,
      "end_seconds": 34.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Only stopping to rest, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.49,
      "end_seconds": 38.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.68,
      "end_seconds": 48.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "It usually comes with a heavy feeling in the left arm. I've had breathlessness on exertion too, uh, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.15,
      "end_seconds": 60.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.47,
      "end_seconds": 65.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Only resting, and it's not much. It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.55,
      "end_seconds": 80.98,
      "duration_seconds": 14.43,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.1,
      "end_seconds": 83.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.84,
      "end_seconds": 88.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Have you had any cough, palpitations or swelling in the ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.68,
      "end_seconds": 91.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.68,
      "end_seconds": 94.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Any pain at rest or fainting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.72,
      "end_seconds": 99.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "I haven't had pain at rest or fainting, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.32,
      "end_seconds": 102.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.14,
      "end_seconds": 104.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.71,
      "end_seconds": 108.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.79,
      "end_seconds": 111.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.41,
      "end_seconds": 116.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.03,
      "end_seconds": 121.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.68,
      "end_seconds": 123.38,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.82,
      "end_seconds": 127.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.48,
      "end_seconds": 134.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the heart disease in your file as well. Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.86,
      "end_seconds": 150.55,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "It's losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'm on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.73,
      "end_seconds": 154.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.36,
      "end_seconds": 156.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.04,
      "end_seconds": 173.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.94,
      "end_seconds": 183.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "So, I had a lump removed from my back years ago. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.14,
      "end_seconds": 187.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.14,
      "end_seconds": 201.72,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.68,
      "end_seconds": 206.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "So, do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.02,
      "end_seconds": 209.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Not that I know, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.93,
      "end_seconds": 214.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.06,
      "end_seconds": 215.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.07,
      "end_seconds": 234.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.95,
      "end_seconds": 248.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.03,
      "end_seconds": 272.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 158 over 101, height 168 centimetres, weight 57 kilos, BMI works out to 20.2, pulse is 83 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.65,
      "end_seconds": 273.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.34,
      "end_seconds": 282.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.47,
      "end_seconds": 293.8,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "Yes, uh, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.72,
      "end_seconds": 299.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.73,
      "end_seconds": 302.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.71,
      "end_seconds": 306.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.62,
      "end_seconds": 317.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.96,
      "end_seconds": 320.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Yes, uh, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.22,
      "end_seconds": 324.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Right, look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.35,
      "end_seconds": 335.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.92,
      "end_seconds": 351.18,
      "duration_seconds": 12.26,
      "text": "Right, that's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.47,
      "end_seconds": 355.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.33,
      "end_seconds": 362.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Putting it all together, it fits best with angina-type chest pain. Gastro-oesophageal reflux is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.22,
      "end_seconds": 365.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.33,
      "end_seconds": 383.65,
      "duration_seconds": 14.32,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with angina-type chest pain do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had tightness in your chest when you walk for two weeks, and no palpitations or pain at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.51,
      "end_seconds": 386.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.61,
      "end_seconds": 395.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "We should do an ECG for chest tightness. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.93,
      "end_seconds": 397.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.46,
      "end_seconds": 423.56,
      "duration_seconds": 25.1,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a lipid profile for cardiovascular risk. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's use GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes, as needed. That's for chest tightness. Let's use atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. That should help with cardiovascular risk. Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.99,
      "end_seconds": 446.3,
      "duration_seconds": 21.31,
      "text": "A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Keep an eye out, and if the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.53,
      "end_seconds": 448.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.19,
      "end_seconds": 455.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.8,
      "end_seconds": 466.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "So, I take the GTN spray, 0.4 milligrams, when the chest tightness comes and take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.64,
      "end_seconds": 471.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.12,
      "end_seconds": 474.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}